{"title":"Career Roadmap · CT Technologist","role":"CT Technologist","summary":"A CT Technologist operates computed tomography equipment to acquire high-quality cross-sectional diagnostic images under the direction and protocols of qualified radiologists and clinical teams.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Medical Imaging Technology - MRI / CT Specialisation"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A CT Technologist operates computed tomography equipment to acquire high-quality cross-sectional diagnostic images under the direction and protocols of qualified radiologists and clinical teams."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical imaging"},{"text":"Patient care"},{"text":"CT equipment operation"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Contrast-procedure support"},{"text":"Image-quality control"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Digital image management"},{"text":"Emergency preparedness"}]},{"type":"p","text":"CT Technologists commonly work in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Diagnostic imaging centres"},{"text":"Trauma centres"},{"text":"Emergency departments"},{"text":"Specialty hospitals"},{"text":"Cancer centres"},{"text":"Academic medical centres"},{"text":"Mobile imaging services"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"CT Technologist is a specialized medical-imaging role. A generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT qualification should not automatically be considered sufficient. Students should complete a recognized medical-imaging/radiography qualification with appropriate clinical training and meet the applicable employer/regulatory requirements. The technologist acquires and optimizes images; diagnosis and interpretation are performed by qualified radiologists/physicians."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","i