ose"},{"text":"Signal-to-noise concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Patient care"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Immobilization"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Special-needs patients"},{"text":"Pediatric considerations"},{"text":"Emergency patients"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — CT Specialization"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the key specialization stage."},{"type":"h","text":"CT fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT scanner components"},{"text":"Gantry"},{"text":"X-ray tube"},{"text":"Detectors"},{"text":"Data acquisition system"},{"text":"Reconstruction"},{"text":"CT numbers/Hounsfield units"},{"text":"Windowing"},{"text":"Slice thickness"},{"text":"Pitch"},{"text":"Rotation time"},{"text":"Scan field of view"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Image planes"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Axial"},{"text":"Coronal"},{"text":"Sagittal"},{"text":"Oblique"},{"text":"3D reconstructions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"CT workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Verification","Clinical Indication","Protocol Selection","Patient Preparation","Positioning","Scout / Localizer","CT Acquisition","Image Reconstruction","Image Quality Check","PACS Transfer","Radiologist Review"]}]},{"heading":"Final Year — Advanced CT Practice","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Advanced CT applications"},{"type":"p","text":"Students should gain exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brain CT"},{"text":"Chest CT"},{"text":"Abdomen CT"},{"text":"Pelvis CT"},{"text":"Spine CT"},{"text":"Musculoskeletal CT"},{"text":"Trauma CT"},{"text":"CT angiography"},{"text":"High-resolution CT"},{"text":"Low-dose CT"},{"text":"Contrast-enhanced CT"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emergency imaging"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn workflows for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Head trauma"},{"text":"Polytrauma"},{"text":"Stroke pathways"},{"text":"Acute abdomen"},{"text":"Pulmonary emergencies"},{"text":"Major vascular emergencies"},{"text":"Exact protocols are institution-specific and are generally performed under established radiology protocols."}]}]},{"heading":"Core Technical Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill Area","Key Competency"],"rows":[[{"text":"CT Physics"},{"text":"X-ray, attenuation & reconstruction"}],[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Cross-sectional anatomy"}],[{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Accurate patient positioning"}],[{"text":"Protocols"},{"text":"Selecting prescribed scan protocols"}],[{"text":"Image Quality"},{"text":"Artifact recognition & optimization"}],[{"text":"Radiation Safety"},{"text":"Dose optimization"}],[{"text":"Contrast"},{"text":"Contrast-procedure support"}],[{"text":"PACS"},{"text":"Image management"}],[{"text":"RIS"},{"text":"Radiology workflow"}],[{"text":"Emergency"},{"text":"Trauma & urgent imaging workflow"}],[{"text":"Patient Care"},{"text":"Communication & monitoring"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Accurate imaging records"}]]}]},{"heading":"CT Physics You Should Understand","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Hounsfield Units"},{"type":"p","text":"CT images represent tissue attenuation using CT numbers."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical conceptual ranges include:"},{"type":"table","header":["Material","Approximate CT Character"],"rows":[[{"text":"Air"},{"text":"Very low"}],[{"text":"Fat"},{"text":"Low"}],[{"text":"Water"},{"text":"Around reference level"}],[{"text":"Soft tissue"},{"text":"Higher"}],[{"text":"Bone"},{"text":"Very high"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact value varies with scanner, protocol and reconstruction."},{"type":"h","text":"Why this matters"},{"type":"p","text":"CT Technologists use knowledge of attenuation and windowing to ensure images are appropriate for clinical interpretation."}]},{"heading":"Windowing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Important concepts include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Window width"},{"text":"Window level"},{"text":"Brain window"},{"text":"Lung window"},{"text":"Bone window"},{"text":"Soft-tissue window"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"flow","items":["Raw CT Data","Reconstruction","Window / Level Adjustment","Clinical Image Series"]},{"type":"p","text":"The technologist ensures appropriate image series are produced; diagnostic interpretation remains the radiologist's responsibility."}]},{"heading":"CT Protocol Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong CT Technologist should understand why protocols differ."},{"type":"h","text":"Examples"},{"type":"h","text":"Head CT"},{"type":"p","text":"Considerations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brain coverage"},{"text":"Slice thickness"},{"text":"Brain/bone reconstruction"},{"text":"Trauma requirements"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Chest CT"},{"type":"p","text":"Considerations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lung coverage"},{"text":"Breath-hold"},{"text":"Thin-section reconstruction"},{"text":"Low-dose protocols where appropriate"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Abdomen/Pelvis"},{"type":"p","text":"Considerations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scan range"},{"text":"Contrast phase"},{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Breath-hold"},{"text":"Reconstruction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"CT Angiography"},{"type":"p","text":"Considerations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Contrast timing"},{"text":"Bolus tracking"},{"text":"Acquisition timing"},{"text":"Reconstruction"},{"text":"Dose optimization"},{"text":"The actual protocol is determined by the clinical indication and institutional/radiologist-approved protocol."}]}]},{"heading":"Radiation Safety","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Radiation protection is one of the most important CT competencies."},{"type":"h","text":"Core principles"},{"type":"flow","items":["Justification","Optimization","Dose Reduction","Image Quality Appropriate for Purpose"]},{"type":"h","text":"Technologist responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Verify patient identity"},{"text":"Confirm requested examination"},{"text":"Avoid unnecessary repeat scans"},{"text":"Follow approved protocols"},{"text":"Optimize exposure"},{"text":"Use appropriate positioning"},{"text":"Follow radiation-protection procedures"},{"text":"Monitor dose indicators"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important concept"},{"type":"h","text":"ALARA — As Low As Reasonably Achievable"},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is to obtain diagnostically useful images while minimizing unnecessary radiation exposure."}]},{"heading":"Contrast-Enhanced CT","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"CT Technologists may support contrast-enhanced examinations according to institutional protocols and scope."},{"type":"h","text":"Knowledge required"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Contrast agents"},{"text":"Patient screening"},{"text":"Relevant history"},{"text":"Previous reactions"},{"text":"Renal-function information where required by protocol"},{"text":"IV access"},{"text":"Injection systems"},{"text":"Contrast timing"},{"text":"Adverse-reaction recognition"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Screening","Clinical / Safety Verification","IV Access","Contrast Administration","CT Acquisition","Patient Observation","Documentation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The technologist should follow local protocols and immediately escalate suspected contrast reactions to the clinical team."}]},{"heading":"CT Artifacts","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A CT Technologist should recognize common artifacts."},{"type":"h","text":"Examples"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motion artifact"},{"text":"Beam-hardening"},{"text":"Metal artifact"},{"text":"Ring artifact"},{"text":"Partial-volume effect"},{"text":"Stair-step artifact"},{"text":"Photon starvation"},{"text":"Truncation"},{"text":"Misregistration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Artifact workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Artifact Detected","Identify Cause","Assess Clinical Impact","Correct Position / Protocol Wher