 should ideally demonstrate:"},{"type":"h","text":"Imaging"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT physics"},{"text":"Cross-sectional anatomy"},{"text":"CT protocols"},{"text":"Image reconstruction"},{"text":"Artifact recognition"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Contrast-procedure support"},{"text":"Emergency imaging"},{"text":"Basic life support"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Safety"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation protection"},{"text":"Dose optimization"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Patient identification"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT console"},{"text":"PACS"},{"text":"RIS"},{"text":"DICOM"},{"text":"EMR/HIS"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CTA fundamentals"},{"text":"3D reconstruction"},{"text":"Spectral CT awareness"},{"text":"AI-assisted imaging awareness"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical Imaging Foundation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Cross-Sectional Anatomy"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"CT Physics"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"CT Protocols"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Patient Positioning"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Radiation Safety"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Contrast Safety"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Image Quality & Artifact Management"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"PACS / RIS / DICOM"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Emergency CT"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"3D Reconstruction"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"CTA / Spectral CT Awareness"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"AI-Assisted Imaging"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Patient Communication"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Recognized Medical Imaging/Radiography Qualification","Clinical Imaging Training","CT Internship","CT Technologist","Advanced CT Protocols","Senior CT Technologist","CT Specialist / Applications Specialist / Imaging Supervisor"]},{"type":"flow","items":["For maximum employability, combine strong CT physics","cross-sectional anatomy","protocol knowledge","radiation safety","contrast workflow","image-quality optimization","PACS/DICOM","emergency CT","3D reconstruction","AI/imaging-informatics awareness."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Career-fitment mapping note","text":"This role should be mapped specifically to students pursuing a recognized medical imaging/radiography pathway with CT clinical training, rather than presenting a generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT degree as automatically qualifying for CT Technologist employment. The CT Technologist is responsible for safe image acquisition and technical quality; diagnostic interpretation remains the responsibility of the qualified radiologist/physician."}]}]}